@AbySalto.Mid_HostAddress = https://localhost:7221
@email = test@example.com
@password = Password123!

### 1.1. registration — expect 200 OK (first time)
POST {{AbySalto.Mid_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 1.2 user info before logging in — expect 401 unauthorized
GET {{AbySalto.Mid_HostAddress}}/api/auth/manage/info
Accept: application/json

### 1.3 log in using cookie auth — expect 200 and Set-Cookie in headers
POST {{AbySalto.Mid_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login?useCookies=true
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 1.4. current user info — expect 200 with email (Visual Studio uses it's cookie jar)
GET {{AbySalto.Mid_HostAddress}}/api/auth/manage/info
Accept: application/json
# Cookie: {{authCookie}}

### 1.5. incorrect password — expect 401
POST {{AbySalto.Mid_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login?useCookies=true
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "WrongPassword123!"
}


### 2.1 get all products - expect 200 with products
GET {{AbySalto.Mid_HostAddress}}/api/products
Accept: application/json

### 2.2 get existing product - expect 200 with product
GET {{AbySalto.Mid_HostAddress}}/api/products/42
Accept: application/json

### 2.3 get non-existing product - expect 404
GET {{AbySalto.Mid_HostAddress}}/api/products/123456789
Accept: application/json

### 2.4 get product with 0 id  - expect 400 bad request
GET {{AbySalto.Mid_HostAddress}}/api/products/0
Accept: application/json

### 2.5 get product with negative id  - expect 400 bad request
GET {{AbySalto.Mid_HostAddress}}/api/products/-5
Accept: application/json
